WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:04.650
Robb Stark: The Starks reigned as kings for
thousands of years, even withstanding the

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:07.000
invasion of the Andals.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:13.170
As the southern kingdoms fell, and the Children
were driven away, the North stood strong,

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.539
maintaining its religious customs and its
way of life.

00:00:16.539 --> 00:00:21.320
Eventually, the reign of the Kings of Winter
came to an end with the coming of Aegon the

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.359
Conqueror.

00:00:23.359 --> 00:00:28.439
After Aegon and his dragons destroyed the
armies of the Reach and the Rock at the Field

00:00:28.439 --> 00:00:35.320
of Fire, King Torrhen Starkbent the knee and
swore fealty to the Targaryen dynasty in order

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:39.660
to spare the destruction of Winterfell and
his people.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.960
He was forever after known as "the King Who
Knelt."

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:48.670
As a reward for his submission, Aegon named
TorrhenLord of Winterfell and Warden of the

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:49.670
North.

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:55.050
Sansa Stark: The North is the oldest and largest
of the Seven Kingdoms, but House Stark has

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.110
not always held it.

00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:01.450
When Bran the Builder raised Winterfell and
founded our line, we were vassals to the Barrow

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:17.240
Kings, who claimed descent from the First
King and thus dominion over all 

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:22.950
the First Men.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:27.100
But after the Long Night, it was our house
who built the Wall and set the Night's Watch

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:32.090
to guard the realms of men whilst our king
sat in his barrow.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:37.850
My ancestors eventually revolted, waging what
singers call the Thousand Years War to free

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:39.810
our lands.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:44.370
Other families joined us, recognizing that
the North is a cold and hard land and needed

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.970
a king who served its people before himself.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:55.290
Finally, the last Barrow King bent the knee,
and House Stark became the Kings of Winter.

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:57.830
Yet we were kings in name only.

00:01:57.830 --> 00:02:02.219
For by then, the North had fractured into
petty kingdoms, and my ancestors would struggle

00:02:02.219 --> 00:02:05.730
to unite it again for thousands of years.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:10.390
Rodrik Stark wrestled an Ironborn lord for
Bear Island and granted it to House Mormont

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:12.050
when he won.

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:16.890
A younger son of our family, Karlon Stark,
won his own keep after he put down a rebellion

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:21.300
and founded House Karstark, one of the most
powerful in the North.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:25.519
When the Manderlys were exiled from the Reach,
my ancestors shielded them and gave them a

00:02:25.519 --> 00:02:31.050
home at the mouth of the White Knife in return
for holding the river against pirates and

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.050
invaders.

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:35.380
Now they're one of the wealthiest houses in
the North.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:40.300
I'm not so naive to pretend that the entire
North welcomed Stark rule.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:45.270
The last Warg King was slain at Sea Dragon
Point along with all his sons and beasts.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:49.660
The last Marsh King died at the hands of King
Rickard Stark, and House Reed has held the

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:52.550
swamps of the Neck ever since.

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:56.129
Houses Greenwood, Towers, Amber, Frost.

00:02:56.129 --> 00:03:00.659
None survive today as more than names in dusty
old books.

00:03:00.659 --> 00:03:05.590
But my ancestors never wanted to destroy their
foes root and stem.

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:09.520
The Umbers of Last Hearth and the Glovers
of Deepwood Mottebent the knee and became

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:12.319
loyal vassals of House Stark.

00:03:12.319 --> 00:03:17.489
The Red Kings of House Bolton wore cloaks
made from the skins of Stark princes they'd

00:03:17.489 --> 00:03:23.269
flayed, and one of the Boltons was even known
as the Redarm because he liked to plunge an

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:29.610
arm into the bellies of captive Starks and
pull out their entrails with his bare hand.

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:33.820
The North deserved to be wiped clean of them.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:39.010
Yet my ancestors spared them after their defeat
because they believed the North couldn't afford

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:41.670
to fight itself any longer.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:44.360
Time soon proved them right.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:49.430
When the Andals swept into Westeros, they
obliterated all the kingdoms of the First

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:51.970
Men except the North.

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:57.860
Each of the southern kingdoms fought the invaders
on its own, but the North fought as one.

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:01.301
When the Andals tried to sail on the White
Knife, the Manderlys fell on their ships.

00:04:01.301 --> 00:04:07.610
When the Andals tried to march an army through
the Neck, the Reeds fell on their soldiers.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:13.230
King Theon Stark even sailed his own army
to the Andalhomeland for vengeance and slew

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.870
hundreds of Andal warriors.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:22.220
When he returned, he planted their heads on
spikes along our coasts — a warning to other

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.250
would-be conquerors.

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:29.410
The warning was heeded for thousands of years,
until Aegon the Conqueror.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:32.000
The south had already fallen to Aegon and
his dragons.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.250
Only the North remained.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:39.500
My ancestor, King Torrhen Stark, marched the
North down to the Trident and beheld Aegon's

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:45.930
army, larger than Torrhen's own by half and
with three dragons circling overhead.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:51.690
Many northern bannermen wanted to attack anyway,
claiming northern valor would carry the day.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:55.130
Others wanted to fall back to Moat Cailin
and make a stand there.

00:04:55.130 --> 00:05:00.240
But Torrhen had heard how the armies of the
Rock and the Reach had burned on the Field

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:05.470
of Fire and had seen the fires still glowing
beneath the rubble of Harrenhal.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:12.669
He knelt and laid his ancient crown as Aegon's
feet and rose a king no more but Lord of Winterfell

00:05:12.669 --> 00:05:15.479
and Warden of the North.

00:05:15.479 --> 00:05:21.100
Some Northerners still sneer at my ancestor
as "The King Who Knelt," forgetting that because

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:24.229
of Torrhen, they're alive today to sneer.

00:05:24.229 --> 00:05:28.190
Their ancestors didn't leave their burned
bones at the Trident, and their twisted swords

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:30.350
didn't fill Aegon'snew throne.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:35.440
Roose Bolton: Brandon the Builder, founder
of House Stark, raised Winterfell with giants

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.530
over eight thousand years ago.

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:40.520
Or so nursemaids tell all the children of
the North.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:44.760
The children nod, wide-eyed, unaware of the
lesson forced on them.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:49.560
That if even giants obeyed a Stark, so too
should they.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:54.620
But like every other castle, Winterfell was
built in pieces over thousands of years.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:58.450
The First Men settled there because of the
hot springs that bubbled through the ground.

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:03.310
The water and the heat helped them survive
the Northern winters, and they built defenses

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:05.760
to keep it for themselves.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:11.229
Nobody raised the castle all at once, probably
nobody meant to raise a castle at all.

00:06:11.229 --> 00:06:15.880
In those days, the Starks were not the greatest
house in the North, and Winterfell was not

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:17.750
the greatest castle.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:22.300
Barrowton was the oldest, dating to the First
King, and the Starks fought the Barrow Kings

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:24.479
for a thousand years.

00:06:24.479 --> 00:06:29.190
Greywater Watch was, like the crannogmen themselves,
the strangest.

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:31.759
Only marriage subdued its Marsh Kings.

00:06:31.759 --> 00:06:37.270
But the greatest rival to Winterfell was always
the Dreadfort, and my ancestors, the Red Kings

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:38.850
of House Bolton.

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:43.940
If tales can be believed, we fought from the
Long Night until the Andals came.

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:49.169
Because of us, Winterfell raised its first
walls, but we took and burned that castle

00:06:49.169 --> 00:06:50.169
anyway.

00:06:50.169 --> 00:06:53.850
Winterfell built more keeps, more walls, more
guard towers.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:57.629
They expanded the granaries and larders to
survive our sieges.

00:06:57.629 --> 00:07:02.670
They tended the godswood to win favor with
the Old Gods against us.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:07.330
As the castle grew, more farmers and villagers
flocked every winter from across the North

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:11.270
to huddle under its walls, raising the winter
town.

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:15.990
In the spring these villagers would find themselves
marching in the Stark armies to fight against

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:16.990
us.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:21.720
The greatness of Winterfell is as much our
doing as the Starks.

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:27.000
But in the end, neither its stone walls nor
its tall keeps and iron gates could save Winterfell.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.100
At its height, it could have lasted a year
under heavy siege.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:35.490
But a handful of ironbornseized it in the
night, while its lord, the King in the North,

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:37.319
was playing in the south.

00:07:37.319 --> 00:07:39.169
My dagger ended his reign.

00:07:39.169 --> 00:07:44.690
Jon Snow: As a boy, looking out from my father's
castle, I thought the sun could never set

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:45.690
on the North.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:46.690
So vast did it seem.

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:49.810
A part of me still does.

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:54.810
The North is by far the largest of the Seven
Kingdoms and can fit the other six inside

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:55.810
it.

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:57.060
Not that the others care.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:02.379
Cold and damp, that's how the southerners
see the North.

00:08:02.379 --> 00:08:07.870
But without the cold, a man can't appreciate
the fire in his hearth.

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:11.680
Without the rain, a man can't appreciate the
roof over his head.

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:19.500
Let the south have its sun, flowers, and affectations,
we Northerners have home.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:26.500
Mine was once Winterfell, the ancient seat
of my father's family, House Stark, who have

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:30.910
ruled the North since the First Men and were
once the Kings of Winter.

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:37.570
Growing up, Lady Catelyn made sure I knew
I wasn't a Stark, no matter how much blood

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:40.140
I shared with her trueborn children.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:45.430
But where their name rules over the North,
mine is the North.

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:47.010
Snow.

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:51.530
Our lands stretches from the Wall down to
the Neck, a narrow land that divides it from

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:53.870
the rest of Westeros.

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:58.630
Legend has it that the Children of the Forestflooded
it in their war against the First Men.

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:02.200
If that's true, every Northman owes them a
debt of gratitude.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:07.790
The swamps of the Neck are as good as the
Wall for keeping out unwelcome armies.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:11.269
And if the swamps don't deter you, the crannogmen
should.

00:09:11.269 --> 00:09:18.000
Small, shy people who rarely leave those swamps
and who follow House Reed, the gatekeepers

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:23.680
of the North, and among the most important
and loyal bannermen of House Stark.

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:25.270
Also a bit strange.

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:29.300
I heard their oath of fealty once as a child.

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:31.440
It's is like no other lords'.

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:40.019
Ancient and dark, they swear by earth and
water, by bronze and iron, and by ice and

00:09:40.019 --> 00:09:41.320
fire.

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:47.250
Where House Reed holds the gate to the North,
House Manderly holds the port.

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:51.750
White Harbor, the closest thing to a southern
city we have governed by the closest thing

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:53.890
to a southern family we have.

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:57.660
Generations ago, the Manderlys were driven
from the Reach, but the Starks gave them their

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:59.960
land in return for fealty.

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:05.330
Now White Harbor is the richest city of the
North, and the Manderlys the richest family.

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:11.540
Not in gold and silver like their southern
counterparts, but in fish and grain and trade.

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:15.850
As for the other great Northern houses, the
Starks brought them into the fold during the

00:10:15.850 --> 00:10:17.240
Age of Heroes.

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:21.730
A Stark wrestled an ironborn for Bear Island
and gave it to the Mormonts.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:26.390
A Stark granted a keep and land to a younger
son, Karlon, in return for putting down a

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:27.390
rebellion.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:31.490
His family then grew up into the Karstarks.

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:36.350
Starks fought the wildlings and their Kings-Beyond-the-Wall
beside the Umbers of Last Hearth, thus earning

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:37.540
their fealty.

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:38.540
Boltons.

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:42.080
Back then, they were the bane of the North.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:46.329
A few were even rumored to wear their enemies'
flayed skins as cloaks.

00:10:46.329 --> 00:10:51.389
But after centuries of war, they too bent
the knee.

00:10:51.389 --> 00:10:56.580
And so House Stark became the Kings in the
North, but never forgot that they weren't

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:57.920
the North.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:04.090
When Aegon and his dragons landed on Westeros,
the Kings of the Rock and the Reach sent all

00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:07.430
of their men to die to defend their grounds.

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:12.149
Torrhen Stark knelt to spare his people the
same fate.

00:11:12.149 --> 00:11:14.559
He placed duty above pride.

